{"id":"magellan-1519","title":"Around the World","explorer":"Ferdinand Magellan and Juan Sebastián Elcano","years":[1519,1522],"calendar":"julian","status":"draft","home":{"name":"Sanlúcar de Barrameda","lat":36.78,"lon":-6.35},"summary":"Five ships sail west to reach the Spice Islands by a strait no one has found, across an ocean no one guessed was so wide. Three years later one ship comes home with eighteen of the 260 or so who left.","sourceNote":"Most of what we know comes from Antonio Pigafetta, a Venetian who sailed as a volunteer and kept a diary, and from the pilot Francisco Albo's log of daily latitudes. Dates are Julian, as recorded; add ten days for the Gregorian calendar.","knownWorld":{"type":"FeatureCollection","note":"Approximate, hand-drawn: the world on Spanish and Portuguese charts in 1519, from the Caribbean and the coast of Brazil to the Río de la Plata, and from Africa round to India, Malacca and the Moluccas.","features":[{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"Europe, the Mediterranean and the Near East"},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-24,66.5],[-12,67],[5,63],[15,69.5],[30,71],[45,67],[60,60],[70,50],[78,40],[88,28],[92,22],[86,19],[80.5,13],[79,8],[76,7],[72,18],[66,24],[58,22],[55,16],[45,12],[43,11],[38,15],[33,22],[28,26],[20,26],[10,27],[0,28],[-8,27],[-13,26.5],[-18.6,27],[-20,32],[-15,36.5],[-32,36],[-32,40.5],[-20,44],[-12,50],[-14,58],[-24,63],[-24,66.5]]]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"The coasts of Africa"},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-19,27.5],[-19,21],[-26,18],[-26,14],[-18,10],[-14,5],[-8,2.5],[0,2.5],[5,1.5],[7,-2],[10,-8],[11,-15],[11.5,-22],[14,-30],[16,-36],[20,-36.5],[27.5,-35.5],[33,-32],[37,-27],[42,-18],[44,-12],[51,-11],[51.5,-20],[48,-26.5],[44,-26],[43,-12],[45,-2],[50,5],[53,12],[48,9],[42,3],[38,-4],[37.5,-10],[38,-17],[33,-24],[29,-30],[26,-32.5],[20,-32],[18,-28],[16,-22],[15,-15],[14,-8],[13,-3],[11,0],[11,3],[9,5],[5,7],[0,7.5],[-5,7.5],[-9,9],[-12,12],[-14,15],[-14,2