 of the Eleven Thousand Virgins"},{"date":"1520-10-22","lat":-52.45,"lon":-68.45,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1520-10-24","lat":-52.32,"lon":-68.95,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1520-10-26","lat":-52.47,"lon":-69.42,"confidence":"interpolated","place":"First Narrows"},{"date":"1520-10-27","lat":-52.6,"lon":-69.68,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1520-10-30","lat":-52.65,"lon":-70.05,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1520-11-02","lat":-52.72,"lon":-70.4,"confidence":"interpolated","place":"Second Narrows"},{"date":"1520-11-05","lat":-53.15,"lon":-70.65,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1520-11-08","lat":-53.6,"lon":-70.85,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1520-11-12","lat":-53.88,"lon":-71.25,"confidence":"interpolated","place":"off Cape Froward"},{"date":"1520-11-15","lat":-53.8,"lon":-71.65,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1520-11-18","lat":-53.62,"lon":-72.3,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1520-11-21","lat":-53.3,"lon":-72.85,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1520-11-24","lat":-52.98,"lon":-73.4,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1520-11-26","lat":-52.78,"lon":-74.15,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1520-11-28","lat":-52.6,"lon":-74.75,"confidence":"documented","sourceId":"albo","place":"Cape Deseado: the Pacific"},{"date":"1520-12-01","lat":-48,"lon":-77,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"albo"},{"date":"1520-12-08","lat":-38.5,"lon":-77.5,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"albo"},{"date":"1520-12-18","lat":-32.3,"lon":-80.5,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"albo"},{"date":"1520-12-28","lat":-25.5,"lon":-92,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"albo"},{"date":"1521-01-10","lat":-19,"lon":-114,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"albo"},{"date":"1521-01-24","lat":-14.85,"lon":-138.8,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"albo","place":"San Pablo (Puka-Puka?)"},{"date":"1521-02-04","lat":-10.6,"lon":-151,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"albo","place":"Los Tiburones"},{"date":"1521-02-13","lat":0,"lon":-158.5,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"albo","place":"crossing the line"},{"date":"1521-02-25","lat":9,"lon":-172,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"albo"},{"date":"1521-03-05","lat":13.05,"lon":144.5,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1521-03-06","lat":13.28,"lon":144.6,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"albo","place":"Guam"},{"date":"1521-03-09","lat":13.28,"lon":144.6,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"pigafetta"},{"date":"1521-03-16","lat":11.1,"lon":125.95,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"albo","place":"off Samar"},{"date":"1521-03-17","lat":10.72,"lon":125.8,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"pigafetta","place":"Homonhon"},{"date":"1521-03-25","lat":10.4,"lon":125.45,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1521-03-28","lat":9.92,"lon":125.1,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"pigafetta","place":"Limasawa"},{"date":"1521-04-04","lat":9.92,"lon":125.1,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"pigafetta"},{"date":"1521-04-05","lat":10.05,"lon":124.6,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1521-04-06","lat":10.35,"lon":124.25,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1521-04-07","lat":10.3,"lon":123.95,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"pigafetta","place":"Cebu"},{"date":"1521-05-01","lat":10.3,"lon":123.95,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"pigafetta"},{"date":"1521-05-03","lat":9.75,"lon":123.7,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"pigafetta","place":"off Bohol: the Concepción is burned"},{"date":"1521-05-10","lat":8.95,"lon":123.25,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1521-06-02","lat":8.5,"lon":121,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"bergreen","place":"the Sulu Sea"},{"date":"1521-06-21","lat":8.75,"lon":117.95,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"pigafetta","place":"Palawan"},{"date":"1521-07-09","lat":5.1,"lon":114.85,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"pigafetta","place":"Brunei"},{"date":"1521-07-29","lat":5.1,"lon":114.85,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"pigafetta"},{"date":"1521-08-05","lat":6.3,"lon":115.6,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1521-08-10","lat":7.3,"lon":116.4,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1521-08-15","lat":7.35,"lon":116.95,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"bergreen","place":"careening off north Borneo"},{"date":"1521-09-27","lat":7.35,"lon":116.95,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"bergreen"},{"date":"1521-09-30","lat":7.48,"lon":117.4,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1521-10-10","lat":6.2,"lon":120,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1521-10-20","lat":6.25,"lon":121.6,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1521-10-24","lat":5.9,"lon":123.5,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1521-10-28","lat":5.3,"lon":125.2,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"pigafetta","place":"Sarangani"},{"date":"1521-11-03","lat":2.5,"lon":126.4,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1521-11-08","lat":0.7,"lon":127.33,"confidence":"documented","sourceId":"pigafetta","place":"Tidore, in the Moluccas"}]},{"mode":"sea","vessel":"Victoria","points":[{"date":"1521-11-08","lat":0.7,"lon":127.33,"confidence":"documented","sourceId":"pigafetta"},{"date":"1521-12-21","lat":0.7,"lon":127.33,"confidence":"documented","sourceId":"pigafetta","place":"the Victoria sails under Elcano"},{"date":"1522-01-02","lat":-1,"lon":126.9,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1522-01-08","lat":-2.9,"lon":127.3,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1522-01-12","lat":-3.9,"lon":127.55,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1522-01-18","lat":-7.3,"lon":125.4,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1522-01-20","lat":-8.55,"lon":125.3,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1522-01-22","lat":-8.65,"lon":124,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1522-01-24","lat":-9.4,"lon":123.25,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1522-01-26","lat":-10.1,"lon":123.45,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"pigafetta","place":"Timor"},{"date":"1522-02-11","lat":-10.1,"lon":123.45,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"pigafetta"},{"date":"1522-02-12","lat":-10,"lon":123,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1522-02-20","lat":-16,"lon":113,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"albo"},{"date":"1522-03-10","lat":-30,"lon":90,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"albo"},{"date":"1522-03-25","lat":-38,"lon":75,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"albo"},{"date":"1522-04-15","lat":-38,"lon":52,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"albo"},{"date":"1522-05-08","lat":-36.5,"lon":30,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"albo"},{"date":"1522-05-19","lat":-35.2,"lon":18.8,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"albo","place":"rounding the Cape of Good Hope"},{"date":"1522-06-01","lat":-20,"lon":6,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"albo"},{"date":"1522-06-08","lat":0,"lon":-6,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"pigafetta","place":"crossing the line"},{"date":"1522-06-25","lat":9,"lon":-20,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1522-07-09","lat":14.88,"lon":-23.6,"confidence":"documented","sourceId":"pigafetta","place":"Santiago, Cape Verde"},{"date":"1522-07-14","lat":14.88,"lon":-23.6,"confidence":"documented","sourceId":"pigafetta"},{"date":"1522-07-15","lat":14.75,"lon":-23.85,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1522-07-17","lat":15.4,"lon":-24.1,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1522-08-10","lat":30,"lon":-32,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"albo"},{"date":"1522-08-28","lat":38.5,"lon":-24,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"albo","place":"by the Azores"},{"date":"1522-09-04","lat":36.9,"lon":-9.4,"confidence":"reconstructed","sourceId":"pigafetta","place":"Cape St Vincent"},{"date":"1522-09-05","lat":36.85,"lon":-8,"confidence":"interpolated"},{"date":"1522-09-06","lat":36.8,"lon":-6.45,"confidence":"documented","sourceId":"pigafetta","place":"Sanlúcar de Barrameda"}]}],"moments":[{"date":"1519-09-20","lat":36.8,"lon":-6.45,"kind":"turning-point","title":"Five ships","text":"The Trinidad, San Antonio, Concepción, Victoria and Santiago leave Sanlúcar with about 260 men. Magellan, a Portuguese captain sailing for Spain, has told his crews little of where they are going.","isQuote":false,"sourceId":"pigafetta"},{"date":"1519-12-13","lat":-22.95,"lon":-43.15,"kind":"encounter","title":"The bay of Santa Lucía","text":"In the bay that will become Rio de Janeiro the crews trade with the Tupi people, who have had no rain for two months and greet the fleet with rain falling. Pigafetta fills pages with what he sees.","isQuote":false,"sourceId":"pigafetta"},{"date":"1520-01-10","lat":-35.1,"lon":-55.6,"kind":"hardship","title":"Not a strait","text":"The great opening in the coast that Magellan hoped was the passage west is only the mouth of a river, the Río de la Plata. The search moves south into colder water.","isQuote":false,"sourceId":"pigafetta"},{"date":"1520-04-01","lat":-49.35,"lon":-67.55,"kind":"hardship","title":"Mutiny at San Julián","text":"Wintering in a bleak harbor, three of the five captains rise against Magellan. He retakes the ships within a day; one captain is executed and another left marooned when the fleet sails.","isQuote":false,"sourceId":"pigafetta"},{"date":"1520-06-10","lat":-49.35,"lon":-67.55,"kind":"encounter","title":"The Tehuelche","text":"Tall men dressed in guanaco skins come to the shore. The Europeans call them Patagones, giants. Magellan has two of them seized by trickery to take to Spain.","isQuote":false,"sourceId":"pigafetta"},{"date":"1520-10-21","lat":-52.35,"lon":-68.2,"kind":"landfall","title":"The strait","text":"Past a cape they name for the Eleven Thousand Virgins, a channel opens westward. For five weeks the ships thread a maze of fjords between snowy mountains. At night they see fires burning on the land to the south.","isQuote":false,"sourceId":"pigafetta","slowMotion":true},{"date":"1520-11-08","lat":-53.6,"lon":-70.8,"kind":"hardship","title":"The San Antonio turns back","text":"The largest ship, with most of the fleet's food, slips away in the strait and sails home to Spain. Magellan does not know where she has gone.","isQuote":false,"sourceId":"pigafetta"},{"date":"1520-11-28","lat":-52.6,"lon":-74.75,"kind":"landfall","title":"The Pacific","text":"Three ships come out of the strait into an open ocean so calm that they call it the Pacific. It is far wider than any chart showed.","isQuote":false,"sourceId":"pigafetta","slowMotion":true},{"date":"1521-01-24","lat":-14.85,"lon":-138.8,"kind":"journal","title":"An empty island","text":"After two months of open sea they find a small uninhabited island with no anchorage and call it San Pablo. Which atoll it was is still argued.","isQuote":false,"sourceId":"pigafetta","candidates":[{"name":"Puka-Puka","lat":-14.82,"lon":-138.81},{"name":"Fakahina","lat":-15.98,"lon":-140.15}]},{"date":"1521-02-13","lat":0,"lon":-158.5,"kind":"hardship","title":"Ninety-eight days","text":"The biscuit is powder full of worms, the water is yellow and stinking, and men eat the leather off the yards and sawdust and rats. Scurvy kills nineteen men or more.","isQuote":false,"sourceId":"pigafetta"},{"date":"1521-03-06","lat":13.28,"lon":144.6,"kind":"encounter","title":"Guam","text":"Chamorro people paddle out in fast outrigger canoes and take what they want from the ships, by their own ideas of exchange. Magellan answers by burning houses and killing seven men, and names the islands for thieves.","isQuote":false,"sourceId":"pigafetta","slowMotion":true},{"date":"1521-03-28","lat":9.92,"lon":125.1,"kind":"encounter","title":"Enrique speaks","text":"At Limasawa, Magellan's enslaved servant Enrique, taken in Malacca years before, calls out to the people in a canoe, and they understand him. Language has come around the world before any ship has.","isQuote":false,"sourceId":"pigafetta"},{"date":"1521-04-27","lat":10.3,"lon":124,"kind":"turning-point","title":"Mactan","text":"Determined to force the island of Mactan to submit, Magellan wades ashore with a small party and is killed in the shallows by Lapulapu's warriors.","isQuote":false,"sourceId":"pigafetta","slowMotion":true},{"date":"1521-05-01","lat":10.3,"lon":123.95,"kind":"hardship","title":"The banquet at Cebu","text":"Invited to a feast by the ruler of Cebu, more than twenty of the officers are killed. Too few men are left for three ships, and the Concepción is burned.","isQuote":false,"sourceId":"pigafetta"},{"date":"1521-11-08","lat":0.7,"lon":127.33,"kind":"landfall","title":"The Spice Islands","text":"Twenty-seven months after leaving Spain, the two remaining ships anchor at Tidore and fire their guns for joy. The sultan welcomes them, and they load cloves.","isQuote":false,"sourceId":"pigafetta","slowMotion":true},{"date":"1521-12-21","lat":0.7,"lon":127.33,"kind":"turning-point","title":"One ship west","text":"The Trinidad is leaking and stays behind for repairs. Juan Sebastián Elcano sails the Victoria west for Spain, across the Indian Ocean, away from Portuguese ports.","isQuote":false,"sourceId":"pigafetta"},{"date":"1522-05-19","lat":-35.2,"lon":18.8,"kind":"hardship","title":"The Cape","text":"For weeks contrary gales hold the Victoria back from rounding the Cape of Good Hope. The men are starving, and some want to give in and sail for Mozambique.","isQuote":false,"sourceId":"pigafetta"},{"date":"1522-07-09","lat":14.88,"lon":-23.6,"kind":"turning-point","title":"The missing day","text":"Ashore at Cape Verde for food, the men learn it is Thursday. By the careful count Pigafetta has kept, it is Wednesday. Sailing west with the sun, they have lost a day.","isQuote":false,"sourceId":"pigafetta"},{"date":"1522-09-06","lat":36.8,"lon":-6.45,"kind":"landfall","title":"Eighteen men","text":"The Victoria comes back into Sanlúcar, nearly three years after leaving it, with eighteen of her crew. They are the first people known to have sailed all the way around the world.","isQuote":false,"sourceId":"pigafetta","slowMotion":true}],"sources":[{"id":"pigafetta","title":"Magellan's Voyage Around the World","author":"Antonio Pigafetta, translated by James Alexander Robertson, 1906","url":"https://archive.org/search?query=%22magellan%27s+voyage+around+the+world%22+pigafetta+robertson","publicDomain":true},{"id":"albo","title":"Log-book of Francisco Alvo or Alvaro, in The First Voyage Round the World by Magellan","author":"Lord Stanley of Alderley (translator), Hakluyt Society, 1874","url":"https://archive.org/search?query=%22first+voyage+round+the+world+by+magellan%22","publicDomain":true},{"id":"bergreen","title":"Over the Edge of the World: Magellan's Terrifying Circumnavigation of the Globe","author":"Laurence Bergreen, 2003","publicDomain":false}]}